-- title:
--   Base change of the projective Weierstrass model to an R-field
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring and let $V$ be a projective Weierstrass curve over $R$, i.e. a term of `WeierstrassCurve.Projective R`. Write `projModelCR V` for the scheme $\mathrm{Proj}$ of the graded ring obtained from the polynomial ring in three variables over $R$ by quotienting by the homogeneous ideal `projModelHomogeneousIdealCR V` generated by the Weierstrass cubic, with the grading induced from the standard grading by `quotGradingSubmodule`, and write `projModelStrCR V` for its structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} R$, namely the canonical map $\mathrm{Proj} \to \operatorname{Spec}$ of the degree-zero part followed by $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the algebra map $R \to (\text{degree-zero part})$. The assertion is that for every type $K$ in the same universe as $R$, equipped with a field structure and an $R$-algebra structure, the type of isomorphisms of schemes between the pullback of `projModelStrCR V` along $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the ring map $R \to K$ and `projModelCR (V.baseChange K)` is nonempty. Thus only the existence of some isomorphism is asserted, with no compatibility with the two structure morphisms recorded and no canonical choice made.
--
--   This is the base-change (or fibre) property of the projective plane model of a Weierstrass curve: over any $R$-field $K$ the fibre of the model is the model of the base-changed curve, an instance of the functoriality of $\mathrm{Proj}$ for base change of graded rings. It is used as the base-change ingredient in the construction of relative group laws and in the statements about fibres of Weierstrass models over fields of characteristic zero and of characteristic $p$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassProjModel_projModel_pullback_iso_baseChange.lean

import Definitions.Def_WeierstrassCurve_ProjModel

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits NeronModelInfra WeierstrassProjModel

universe u

theorem WeierstrassProjModel.projModel_pullback_iso_baseChange
    {R : Type u} [CommRing R] (V : WeierstrassCurve.Projective R) :
    ∀ (K : Type u) [Field K] [Algebra R K],
      Nonempty (pullback (projModelStrCR V)
          (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap R K)))
        ≅ projModelCR (V.baseChange K)) := by sorry
